 ## Overview
-This method partitions 3D space into non-overlapping tiles to enable distributed NeRF training across multiple GPUs [S1]. It aims to balance compute by ensuring each partition contains a similar amount of spatial content [S1]. Unlike [Block-NeRF](8581-block-nerf.md) and [NeRFPlayer](9440-nerfplayer.md), which partition based on training camera positions, this method partitions space directly using a Probability Density Function (PDF) derived from scene geometry, allowing for finer bounding boxes in regions with more content or frequent capture [S1].
+This method partitions 3D space into non-overlapping tiles to enable distributed NeRF training across multiple GPUs [S1]. It aims to balance compute by ensuring each partition contains a similar amount of spatial content [S1]. Unlike [Block-NeRF](8581-block-nerf.md), [MegaNeRF](8581-meganerf.md), and [NeRFPlayer](9440-nerfplayer.md), which partition based on training camera positions or use uniform grids, this method partitions space directly using a Probability Density Function (PDF) derived from scene geometry, allowing for finer bounding boxes in regions with more content or frequent capture [S1].
 
